<p>Once the inventory is verified, the uncrating process proceeds with extreme care. Electrical and mechanical items require specialized attention. Technicians must test these units for functionality as soon as they are removed from their packaging.</p>
<p>This includes checking power supplies, verifying motor rotations, and ensuring all electronic components are intact and operational. Failure to conduct immediate testing can mask latent defects that may surface later, complicating warranty claims and operational readiness.</p>
<p>Simultaneously, the placement of clean furniture follows a pre-determined layout plan. Furniture items, which are typically sensitive to handling, must be moved to their designated locations without causing scratches or structural damage.</p>
